# ⚠ `external/*`, not `external/`. Excluding the directory itself stops git descending into it,
# so the negations below can never re-match — the classic gitignore trap. Matching the *contents*
# leaves the directory traversable.
external/*
# ... except the two vendored dependencies that are committed on purpose. box3d is v0.1.0 with
# breaking API churn and ExecoSim archives datasets against this code, so the pin must be exact
# bytes rather than a setup.sh download that depends on GitHub still serving a SHA. See
# external/box3d/VENDORED.md and SIMVAL/PhysicsEngineDiscussion/PHYSICS_ENGINE_ANALYSIS.md R1.
!external/box3d/
!external/box3d/**
!external/tinyxml2/
!external/tinyxml2/**
# MuJoCo, vendored 2026-08-18 as a SECOND URDF physics backend alongside Box3D — not a replacement.
# Same reasoning as box3d: the pin must be exact bytes, because a recorded dataset has to be
# attributable to the engine that produced it. See external/mujoco/VENDORED.md.
!external/mujoco/
!external/mujoco/**
# CoACD, vendored 2026-08-19. Approximate convex decomposition, shared by BOTH backends: it is what
# stops a moving concave mesh being simulated as one fat convex hull (Box3DRobot.cpp:330) and what
# makes a mirrored level usable by MuJoCo at all. Same exact-bytes reasoning as the others.
# See external/coacd/VENDORED.md.
!external/coacd/
!external/coacd/**
# Newton, vendored 2026-08-26 as the MPM deformable-terrain solver used by mpm_sidecar/. Same
# exact-bytes reasoning as the others, plus one specific to this dependency: before it was vendored,
# `newton` resolved through a `site-packages/newton.pth` pointing OUTSIDE any repository, so which
# solver ran depended on machine state. `.git` is excluded (124 MB of history against 41 MB of
# source). See external/newton/VENDORED.md.
!external/newton/
!external/newton/**
deps/
cmake_build/

# Eclipse Project file
/.project
/.cproject
/.settings

/boost
/[Ee]igen
/build_debug
/build_release
# Out-of-tree third-party build (build_thirdparty.sh). Separate from build_release because it
# uses Unreal's toolchain rather than the host's - see cmake/cmake-modules/UnrealToolchain.cmake.
/build_thirdparty
# Cooked convex decompositions. Content-addressed binary blobs regenerated on demand -
# they belong WITH a copied plugin (that is why they live under the plugin) but not in
# git: ExoMy alone is 235 parts across 16 files, and they are reproducible from the meshes.
Plugins/AirSim/Saved/ConvexCache/
Unreal/Plugins/AirSim/Saved/ConvexCache/
**/.convex_cache/
/build_mujoco
# MuJoCo's FetchContent cache. ⚠ These are GIT CLONES of qhull, ccd, lodepng, miniz,
# tinyobjloader and tinyxml2 - `git add` on cmake/ will otherwise embed six repositories.
# They are fetched, not vendored; see external/mujoco/VENDORED.md, which records that as
# the weak point of the pin.
/.fetchcontent-cache
/cmake/.fetchcontent-cache
